        "id": 1269501
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-08-03T06:11:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Followup:\n\nWe do not currently handle `TCPC_REG_ALERT_RX_BUF_OVF` anywhere. CL will need to be expanded to accommodate to do that properly.\n\nAlso, as suspected, we have to \"start tcpci_tcpc_alert() from the top\" by virtue of having `tcpm_alert_status(port, \u0026alert)` at L1179. We have no idea if new (non-RX packet) events have occurred while we\u0027re spinning in the `while()` loop.\n\n* For example, `TCPC_REG_ALERT_FAULT` may have been set.\n\nDepending if `tcpci_tcpc_alert()` is edge-triggered or level-triggered, we may need a callback to kick the function off from the top.\n\nAssistance is requested for the proper approach.",
      "parentUuid": "03395d41_61ec5345",
